solution:
**Given:**

If cot θ = dfrac{3}{4}, θ is an acute angle

**Formula used:**

cot θ = dfrac{{adjacent}}{{opposite}}

sin²θ + cos²θ = 1

tan θ = dfrac{{opposite}}{{adjacent}}

**Calculation:**

Given: cot θ = dfrac{3}{4}

⇒ Opposite side = 4, Adjacent side = 3

⇒ Hypotenuse = sqrt{3² + 4²} = sqrt{9 + 16} = sqrt{25} = 5

⇒ sin θ = dfrac{4}{5}, cos θ = dfrac{3}{5}

⇒ tan θ = dfrac{4}{3}

sin θ + cos θ - tan θ = dfrac{4}{5} + dfrac{3}{5} - dfrac{4}{3}

⇒ dfrac{4 + 3}{5} - dfrac{4}{3}

⇒ dfrac{7}{5} - dfrac{4}{3}

⇒ dfrac{21 - 20}{15}

⇒ dfrac{1}{15}

**∴ The correct answer is option (1).**
